2/dynamic-query-successor.json\n59\t    sha256: 99fa5512704547be8fb40a46e72fb111731f151b1bacd0cd8b6617abc93a0dbe\n60\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/ossie-relational-bundle/notes/reviews/phase-OB2-r1/review.md\n61\t    sha256: 8ecc9256423dc0158b32c834b64a0157f3ec9641ab0dbeeff46d9c9469824c93\n62\t    note: \"sanitized; the reviewer's original bytes are 50e188ef9302c5992a6de9ed1dc047bcaf5717aa1554cdb7b9bfc4f00de0af8b, bound by run.json\"\n63\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/ossie-relational-bundle/notes/reviews/phase-OB2-r1/SANITIZATION.md\n64\t    sha256: 26941c7f96caefc9e67fce2c3f803d55d25111e2d3b7adf2993e99f6e802bbd9\n65\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/ossie-relational-bundle/notes/reviews/phase-OB2-r1/FINDINGS.md\n66\t    sha256: 7d0f36b01140df8ea85d12876b5e4e84aeb6f87cf099825a991e0f1e0a7c534e\n67\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/ossie-relational-bundle/notes/reviews/phase-OB2-r2/review.md\n68\t    sha256: 78f774e204c57c6eb13ead4379bf2ad78eeceadf7662d11c94a71876ae79fd67\n69\t    note: \"sanitized; the reviewer's original bytes are f1a1b819a2ffa0d02979ea7867e5f6b3e5313f6f2f9f8fbd25eedd767fe8e6d4, bound by run.json\"\n70\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/ossie-relational-bundle/notes/reviews/phase-OB2-r2/SANITIZATION.md\n71\t    sha256: 80d86d5a613ff7691781959bf02e465f701c49f6c18519d045ae6a10b9848bd6\n72\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/ossie-relational-bundle/notes/reviews/phase-OB2-r2/FINDINGS.md\n73\t    sha256: 9f30eb372d2993c6de80b79c17df3a73f57972902575fdfca3de63020d8e18d4\n74\t---\n75\t\n76\t# Phase OB2: the Halpin relational mapping (`gnd.rmap`)\n77\t\n78\t## Claim\n79\t\n80\t- **Library.** `gnd.rmap.map_model(model, *, variant=RmapVariant.HALPIN)`\n81\t  maps a loaded model to a `RelationalSchema`: tables, ordered columns,\n82\t  primary keys, unique keys, ordered composite foreign keys, and an unmapped\n83\t  list with a closed set of reasons. `dispositions(model, schema)` is the one\n84\t  walk: exactly one row for every fact type and every constraint (plan §0\n85\t  rule 4). No CLI, no Ossie file and no DDL change (§9).\n86\t- **Corpus.** All 25 owner-approved corpus cases equal their hand-derived\n87\t  answers under HALPIN, and cases 07, 08 and 15 also under ALTERNATE (T6).\n88\t  No approved answer changed.\n89\t- **Totality** (OB2-C1). Every standalone census and fixture model the loader\n90\t  admits maps under both variants without raising, including adversarial\n91\t  identification cycles (T1, T1b).\n92\t- **One walk.** Every fact type and constraint address appears exactly once\n93\t  in `dispositions` over census and corpus (T2). A missing row raises rather\n94\t  than defaulting (IF1).\n95\t- **Determinism** (OB2-C3). Reversed declaration order and another source\n96\t  path give an equal schema and equal dispositions (T3, T3b, R3).\n97\t- **Time** (OB2-C4). The 1,400-entity, 4,500-fact-type model maps within\n98\t  the recorded bound; the 5× model's time ratio is under 12 (T4, T4b), and\n99\t  composite identification does not grow superlinearly (R9).\n100\t- **D5** (OB2-C5). Both variants are measured over 66 models\n101\t  ([measurement](notes/OB2-variant-measurement.md)); the owner ruled HALPIN\n102\t  ([D5 gate](007-OB2-D5-gate.md)). ALTERNATE stays behind the internal switch.\n103\t- **Normative home** (plan §0 rule 5). The rules are in\n104\t  `representation-format.md` § \"Relational mapping (Rmap)\", before\n105\t  \"Ossie interchange\".\n106\t- **Homes.** `gnd.rmap` is assigned layer `model` in `tools/gnd_layers.json`\n107\t  and indexed as `model.relational_mapping`. Its model reads go through\n108\t  `ModelIndex`; its dynamic-subscript census is a counted successor delta\n109\t  (IF6), and no query exception is widened.\n110\t\n111\t## Gate\n112\t\n113\tThe front matter gives each command and its exit verbatim.\n114\t\n115\t**Known red.** `tests/test_development_scaffold.py::test_reference_closure_and_declared_bootstrap`\n116\tfails because `.agents/skills/review-pr/SKILL.md` cannot resolve\n117\t`../process-phase/references/review-tool.md`. That is a discovery-link\n118\tlayout this worktree has not adopted (AGENTS.md:\n119\t`uv run gnd install --symlink --project --force`). OB2 is cut from the same\n120\tbase, `a7847f2b`, on which the OB1 record proved this test fails with no\n121\tphase diff applied (`1 failed in 0.47s`), and OB2 touches no part of that\n122\tlayout.\n123\t\n124\t## Review\n125\t\n126\tThere was one reviewer, Codex, run through `review_tool.py` with a read-only\n127\tsandbox and effort high, in two rounds. **One reviewer is one reviewer.**\n128\t\n129\t### Round 1, base `e7af6f50` to head `af34a54e`\n130\t\n131\t| Item | Value |\n132\t|---|---|\n133\t| Review | [review.md](notes/reviews/phase-OB2-r1/review.md), sha256 `50e188ef…af8b` as written, `8ecc9256…9c93` after path sanitization ([SANITIZATION.md](notes/reviews/phase-OB2-r1/SANITIZATION.md)) |\n134\t| Verdict | CHANGES_REQUESTED, with nine findings |\n135\t| Ledger | [FINDINGS.md](notes/reviews/phase-OB2-r1/FINDINGS.md) |\n136\t\n137\t| Id | Class | Reproduced | Disposition |\n138\t|---|---|---|---|\n139\t| F1 | blocking | yes (R1) | fixed: the Rmap selects the confirmed, alethic, preferred external uniqueness (RR1) |\n140\t| F2 | blocking | yes (R2) | fixed: duplicate uniqueness constraints form one key, preferred if any is |\n141\t| F3 | blocking | yes (R3) | fixed: unique keys sort by column position |\n142\t| F4 | blocking | yes (R4) | fixed: an external uniqueness within one table is a unique key |\n143\t| F5 | blocking | yes (R5) | fixed: a narrower objectified uniqueness is a unique key |\n144\t| F6 | blocking | yes (R6) | fixed: under ALTERNATE, an inheriting subtype's supertype gets a table |\n145\t| F7 | hardening | yes (R7) | fixed: a role played by a tabled value type is a foreign key |\n146\t| F8 | blocking | yes (R8) | fixed: an absorbed unary column is nullable |\n147\t| F9 | blocking | yes (R9) | fixed: identifiers are indexed once per model |