es,\n181\trole names with digits, answer file names) found no breaking input.\n182\t\n183\t**The round-2 repaired bytes are not reviewed.** Round 1 found nine\n184\tfindings and round 2 eight, all in edge combinations of identification,\n185\texternal uniqueness and subtypes; the rounds are not yet converging to zero.\n186\t\n187\t## Refactoring review\n188\t\n189\t**Refactor EXECUTED.**\n190\t- **What (RR9):** the role-to-column map was held as text keys and split\n191\t  apart again. It is now a dictionary from fact type to role to columns, and\n192\t  the constraint index is passed in rather than parsed out of its address\n193\t  (AGENTS.md, \"General solutions\").\n194\t- **Behaviour:** preserved; the corpus and every census row are unchanged.\n195\t- **Gate:** the same focused gate and guard block above.\n196\t\n197\t**Seen and deferred.**\n198\t- `export/ossie.py` and `gnd.rmap` each decide \"confirmed alethic\"\n199\t  uniqueness. OB3 edits `export/ossie.py` and should make it consume the\n200\t  Rmap's dispositions (spec §9). Row OB2-Q1.\n201\t- `refscheme.reference_identity` takes the first external uniqueness\n202\t  anchored on an entity, whatever its `preferred` flag and status, and\n203\t  rebuilds a map per call. The Rmap no longer uses it (RR1), but its other\n204\t  callers keep that behaviour. Row OB2-Q2.\n205\t\n206\t## Refuted premises and findings\n207\t\n208\tThe spec's §13 (IF1–IF10) and §14 (RR1–RR9) list them all. The ones that\n209\tchange an earlier document:\n210\t\n211\t- **Plan §2.3 rule 2** groups n−1 uniqueness of n-aries into an entity\n212\t  table. That is not Halpin and has no table to group into. Corrected by S5\n213\t  at the spec gate.\n214\t- **Plan §2.3 on \"no uniqueness\".** The plan did not cover the majority\n215\t  case: 119 of 226 census fact types declare no uniqueness. S1 covers it.\n216\t- **Plan OB2-C4's 10× scale** cannot load under `MAX_MODEL_BYTES` (IF4).\n217\t  T4b runs at 5×.\n218\t- **Spec §6 reuse table** said composite identification reuses `refscheme`.\n219\t  It cannot: wrong selection (F1) and quadratic cost (F9). Replaced by RR1,\n220\t  accepted at the D5 gate.\n221\t- **Spec S7 and A4** omitted rule 1 from the rules that give an entity a\n222\t  table (IF5), accepted at the D5 gate.\n223\t\n224\tThe plan is not edited here; these go to the milestone-close amendment.\n225\t\n226\t## Open questions\n227\t\n228\t| Id | Question | Target |\n229\t|---|---|---|\n230\t| OB1-Q1 | Carried: should `guard_yaml`'s default `max_bytes` resolve `MAX_BYTES` at call time? OB2 reads no YAML itself. | OB5 or the close sweep |\n231\t| OB2-Q1 | Should `export/ossie.py` take its \"confirmed alethic\" decisions from `gnd.rmap.dispositions` instead of its own predicate? | OB3 |\n232\t| OB2-Q2 | Should `refscheme.reference_identity` honour `preferred` and confirmation, and cache its value-type map, for its other callers? | milestone close sweep, or a separate issue |\n233\t| OB2-Q3 | Round 2 ran (owner: \"Re-review, then PR\"). Should the round-2 repairs (`171665e8`) get a third round, or should OB3's own tests be the next instrument? | owner, before OB3 |\n234\t\n235\t## Boundary\n236\t\n237\t- **Size** (spec §10 estimated about 450 source, 120 normative and 350 test\n238\t  lines):\n239\t  - `rmap.py`: 786 lines, about 1.7× the estimate, from the composite\n240\t    identifier index (RR1), external and objectified unique keys (RR4, RR5),\n241\t    the ALTERNATE supertype tables (RR6) and the round-2 repairs (RR10–RR16).\n242\t  - Normative section: 126 lines.\n243\t  - Tests: `test_rmap.py` 652 lines, plus a 42-line generator; the\n244\t    measurement tool is 94 lines.\n245\t  - Corpus: 25 cases with stories and 28 answer files.\n246\t- **Not done:** no Ossie semantic model or mapping files (OB3), no physical\n247\t  binding (OB4), no docs or skill (OB5), no DDL, no CLI.\n248\t- **Not run:** the opt-in oracle lane, and the evidence and census lanes.\n249\t- **Pull request.** The owner