8bae0ce\n78\t---\n79\t\n80\t# Phase OB3: the relational files (semantic model and mapping)\n81\t\n82\t## Claim\n83\t\n84\t- **Five files by default** (D2 a). `gnd export ossie MODEL --out OUT` writes\n85\t  the ontology, sidecar and loss report as before, plus\n86\t  `OUT.semantic_model.<fmt>` and `OUT.mapping.<fmt>`. `--ontology-only`\n87\t  writes the first three.\n88\t- **The legacy files do not change.** With `--ontology-only`, all 82 census\n89\t  entries equal the OB1 baseline (T6). The default run's three legacy files\n90\t  are the same bytes (OB1 T1, and T6 at the command).\n91\t- **The approved corpus holds.** All seven cases equal their hand-derived\n92\t  files byte for byte in YAML, and in structure in JSON (T1).\n93\t- **Valid against the pins** (OB3-C1). The vendored core-spec accepts every\n94\t  semantic model and the vendored `mapping.json` every mapping, for every\n95\t  scanned model the export maps (844 exports), with cross-document\n96\t  references resolved offline (T2).\n97\t- **Self-consistent** (T3). Every expression names a declared field; every\n98\t  link names a relationship of its concept at the level its arity calls\n99\t  for; every referent follows the ontology's `identify_by`.\n100\t- **One walk** (OB3-C3). Every fact type and constraint appears exactly once\n101\t  in the mapping's `GND` extension. Every carried fact type is named by\n102\t  exactly one link tree or listed in `unmapped_links` with a reason (T4).\n103\t- **Reproducible** (OB3-C4). The five files do not depend on the run or the\n104\t  source path (T5).\n105\t- **Collisions and size** (OB3-C5, C6). A file at any of the five paths\n106\t  exits 11 and publishes nothing (T7). `--max-output-bytes` bounds the\n107\t  semantic model and the mapping, at size minus 1 and at size (T8).\n108\t- **Populations** (OB3-C7, D6). A `sample_population` leaves the semantic\n109\t  model identical and changes only `model_identity` in the mapping; the loss\n110\t  report gains its `population:out-of-scope` rows (T9).\n111\t- **Time** (plan §0 rule 2). At 1,400 entities and 4,500 fact types the five\n112\t  files render in 3.3 s, against 2.6 s for three; the ratio to one fifth of\n113\t  that scale is 5.1 (T10).\n114\t- **Rmap** (E3, E4). A composite identifier needs every component functional\n115\t  on the entity. `RelationalSchema` publishes role placements and\n116\t  identifications (T13, T16).\n117\t- **One home.** The rules are in `representation-format.md` § \"Ossie\n118\t  interchange\", \"Semantic model and mapping\".\n119\t\n120\t## Gate\n121\t\n122\tThe front matter gives each command and its exit verbatim.\n123\t\n124\t**Known red.** `tests/test_development_scaffold.py::test_reference_closure_and_declared_bootstrap`\n125\tfails because `.agents/skills/review-pr/SKILL.md` cannot resolve\n126\t`../process-phase/references/review-tool.md`, a discovery-link layout this\n127\tworktree has not adopted. It failed on the phase base before any OB3 edit:\n128\tthe tree `95ca5a24`, which is main at `fd733185`, was tested before the\n129\tmerges of PRs #264, #266 and #270 and gave `1 failed, 1423 passed`, that\n130\ttest being the failure. OB3 touches no part of that layout.\n131\t\n132\t## Review\n133\t\n134\tThere was one reviewer, Codex, run through `review_tool.py` with a read-only\n135\tsandbox and effort high, over base `39e3d4c3` to head `5f687385`. **One\n136\treviewer is one reviewer.**\n137\t\n138\t| Item | Value |\n139\t|---|---|\n140\t| Review | [review.md](notes/reviews/phase-OB3-r1/review.md), sha256 `607d402f…4b93` as written, `d90fe200…8dc1` after path sanitization ([SANITIZATION.md](notes/reviews/phase-OB3-r1/SANITIZATION.md)) |\n141\t| Verdict | CHANGES_REQUESTED, with five findings |\n142\t| Ledger | [FINDINGS.md](notes/reviews/phase-OB3-r1/FINDINGS.md) |\n143\t\n144\t| Id | Class | Reproduced | Disposition |\n145\t|---|---|---|---|\n146\t| F1 | blocking | yes | fixed: a composite identifier's object mapping reads the table's own key columns |\n147\t| F2 | blocking | yes (crash at 250 roles) | fixed: more than 32 roles is listed as `arity-over-limit`, not nested |\n148\t| F3 | blocking | yes | fixed: foreign-key names are unique in the schema |\n149\t| F4 | hardening | yes | fixed: each `iri` percent-encodes the file name |\n150\t| F5 | completeness | yes (it is IF1) | **open, the owner's** (OB3-Q1) |\n151\t\n152\tEight regression tests were shown failing on the pre-repair bytes before any\n153\tfix. The repairs are commit `110f805a`.\n154\t\n155\tThe reviewer also confirmed: 194 tests over the corpus, census and\n156\tbaselines; validation with sockets blocked and no network attempt; the\n157\tbound at size minus 1 and at size for both new files; identical bytes across\n158\truns and paths; the functional-component rule under both variants; and its\n159\tmatcher probes of the identifier quoting and lexing, with no breaking input.\n160\t\n161\t**The repaired bytes are not reviewed.** No second round ran.\n162\t\n163\t## Refactoring review\n164\t\n165\t**Refactors EXECUTED**, behind the same gates:\n166\t- **One encoder.** The YAML and JSON encoding of the ontology was inline in\n167\t  `render_ossie`. It is now `_encode`, which all five files use. The\n168\t  ontology's bytes are unchanged (the OB1 baseline).\n169\t- **One projection.** `_ontology` became `_project`, which also returns the\n170\t  `OntologyView` the mapping reads, so concept names, role order and\n171\t  `identify_by` are computed once. `_ontology` remains for its two callers.\n172\t\n173\t**Seen and deferred.**\n174\t- The ontology export declares no identifier for a unit-based reference,\n175\t  nor for a subtype inheriting through several supertypes. The mapping\n176\t  cannot cover those (16 fact types in 14 scanned models). Row OB3-Q5.\n177\t- `export/ossie.py` still has its own \"confirmed alethic\" predicate (OB2-Q1),\n178\t  kept by E15.\n179\t- `tests/test_ossie_relational.py` and `tests/test_rmap.py` each scan the\n180\t  fixture models with a small helper of their own. Row OB3-Q6.\n181\t\n182\t## Refuted premises and findings\n183\t\n184\tThe spec's §12 (IF1–IF13), §13 (H1–H4), §14 (B1–B14) and §15 (RR1–RR4) list\n185\tthem all. The ones that change an earlier document:\n186\t\n187\t- **Plan predicate 2 and §5** say the default run always adds the two\n188\t  files. A model that maps to no table cannot have a semantic model, because\n189\t  the pinned core-spec requires a dataset (IF1).\n190\t- **Plan §2.3** says the Rmap takes any preferred external uniqueness as a\n191\t  composite key. The ontology export requires functional components, and so\n192\t  does Halpin; E3 (a) aligned the Rmap.\n193\t- **Spec §6.4** gave value types object mappings. The pinned schema allows\n194\t  them only on entity types (B1).\n195\t- **Spec §6.2** gave one `render_relational` function. The builders are\n196\t  split from the encoder (IF6), and `render_ossie` needs the output file's\n197\t  name (B2).\n198\t- **Spec §6.5 and §6.6** named two reasons and no list for unmapped links.\n199\t  There are three reasons and the list `unmapped_links` (IF2, RR2).\n200\t- **OB2 A11** counted foreign-key names per table pair. They are now unique\n201\t  in the schema (RR3).\n202\t\n203\tThe plan is not edited here; these go to the milestone-close amendment.\n204\t\n205\t## Open questions\n206\t\n207\t| Id | Question | Target |\n208\t|---|---|---|\n209\t| OB3-Q1 | **A model that maps to no table** writes three files and a note (IF1, review F5). Accept that, or refuse such an export unless `--ontology-only` is given? | owner, before OB4 |\n210\t| OB3-Q2 | Accept the three rules implementation and review added: the `unmapped_links` list (IF2), the 32-role limit with reason `arity-over-limit` (RR2), and schema-wide foreign-key names (RR3, amending OB2 A11)? | owner, before OB4 |\n211\t| OB3-Q3 | Run the opt-in oracle lane (T11)? Until it runs, upstream acceptance of the quoted identifiers and of `CASE WHEN` is unconfirmed. | owner |\n212\t| OB3-Q4 | Should the review repairs (`110f805a`) get a second round, or are OB4's tests the next instrument? | owner, before OB4 |\n213\t| OB3-Q5 | Should the ontology export declare identifiers for unit-based references and multi-supertype subtypes, so that the mapping can cover them? | close sweep, or a separate issue |\n214\t| OB3-Q6 | Share one fixture-model scan between the Rmap and relational tests? | OB4, which adds a third test file |\n215\t| OB1-Q1 | Carried: `guard_yaml`'s captured default. | OB5 or the close sweep |\n216\t| OB1-Q2 | Carried: D11, the source cap. At the reporter's scale the generated source is 1.5 MB. | after D10's answer |\n217\t| OB2-Q1, OB2-Q2 | Carried: the duplicated predicate; `refscheme`'s selection. | close sweep |\n218\t\n219\t## Boundary\n220\t\n221\t- **Residuals.**\n222\t  - **NULL semantics (E8).** \"A NULL yields no link\" is GND's reading; Ossie\n223\t    does not define it. Unary fact types and absorbed subtypes depend on it.\n224\t  - **Identifier length (E16).** No name is shortened. None of 3,157 scanned\n225\t    fields exceeds 128 characters.\n226\t  - **`identification-differs`.** 16 fact types in 14 of 422 scanned models\n227\t    have a table and no link mapping.\n228\t- **Size** (spec §10 estimated about 350 renderer, 60 wiring, 40 Rmap, 90\n229\t  normative and 450 test lines):\n230\t  - `ossie_relational.py`: 316 lines.\n231\t  - `ossie.py` and `commands/export.py`: 138 lines added and 26 removed,\n232\t    about 2.3× the estimate, from the ontology view (E12), the encoder and\n233\t    the IRI encoding.\n234\t  - `rmap.py`: 89 added and 5 removed, about 2.2×, from the identification\n235\t    record (IF5).\n236\t  - Normative text: 98 lines.\n237\t  - Tests: `test_ossie_relational.py` 586 lines and the corpus checker 336,\n238\t    about 2× the estimate, mostly the cross-checks that had to exist before\n239\t    the renderer.\n240\t- **Not done:** the physical binding (OB4). The explanation, how-to, export\n241\t  skill and release-note entry (OB5): **they still describe three files.**\n242\t  No import of a semantic model or mapping. No DDL.\n243\t- **Not run:** the opt-in oracle lane (T11), and the evidence and census\n244\t  lanes.\n245\t- **Not pushed.** Branch `claude/ossie-ob3-relational-spec`, cut from main\n246\t  at `fd733185`, has no pull request; opening one is the owner's call.\n247\t- **Approval:** this record approves nothing beyond OB3. Merge is the\n248\t  owner's."}
