{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_YKdP7RJLgAfH0A36x0J64B05","content":"55\t--toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.34.0` offline. Publish a raw create-once bundle\n56\tonly with `--raw --out NEW_DIR`, then run `gnd export lean-verify NEW_DIR --json`.\n57\tCompilation is separately selected with `gnd export lean-compile NEW_DIR\n58\t--executable LAKE --json`; `--elaborate-stubs` records stub elaboration separately.\n59\tNeither operation proves a theorem. The selected positive acyclic finite profile,\n60\trefusals, exact propositions and ceilings are in the export boundary above.\n61\t\n62\t## Ossie interchange\n63\t\n64\tUse `gnd export ossie MODEL --out ONTOLOGY.yaml` to create five files: the\n65\tontology, the `ONTOLOGY.yaml.gnd.json` sidecar, the\n66\t`ONTOLOGY.yaml.loss.json` loss report (move it with `--loss-report`), and the\n67\trelational pair `ONTOLOGY.yaml.semantic_model.yaml` and\n68\t`ONTOLOGY.yaml.mapping.yaml`. `--format json` writes JSON instead. Add\n69\t`--ontology-only` when the user wants the ontology without tables; the run\n70\tthen writes the first three files.\n71\t\n72\tBefore sharing, inspect two lists. The loss report names refused pointers.\n73\tThe mapping's `GND` extension lists every fact type and constraint under\n74\t`dispositions`, each carried or given a reason, and may hold\n75\t`unmapped_links`. Report the entries that carry a reason; never describe\n76\tthem as mapped. Use `--strict` when a refusal should prevent writing the\n77\tbundle.\n78\t\n79\tWhen the user has delivered tables, pass their binding file with\n80\t`--physical-binding FILE`. The semantic model then describes those tables.\n81\tA refused binding exits 3 with a `binding:` rule id and writes nothing.\n82\tRepair the binding. Never edit the model to make a binding pass, and do not\n83\tcombine the option with `--ontology-only`.\n84\t\n85\tAn export stopped by `ossie:output-size` can be rerun with\n86\t`--max-output-bytes N`. Use `--max-input-bytes N` on import for a document\n87\tabove the default bound. Raise a bound only for a size refusal that names\n88\tit, never to get past a different refusal. Outputs are create-once: an\n89\texisting file at any output path exits 11.\n90\t\n91\tKeep the ontology, sidecar and loss report together for a GND round trip\n92\twith `gnd import ossie ONTOLOGY.yaml --out MODEL.json`. Preserve the\n93\tontology bytes so import can verify the sidecar binding. Import reads the\n94\tontology only, not the relational pair. The import report is written to\n95\t`MODEL.json.loss.json` by default, or to the path given by `--loss-report`.\n96\t\n97\tUse the [normative Ossie mapping and file format](../gnd-orm-core/references/representation-format.md#ossie-interchange)\n98\tfor supported declarations, pins, output formats, the relational files, the\n99\tbinding rules and import rules.\n100\tThe ordinary CLI routes run offline. Select any external consumer\n101\tverification separately."}
